{
  "id": "COMPOUND:22238 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "Pironetin appears to interact with the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of molecular pathways, as evidenced by its target relationship with CCRF-HSB-2, which is a target of multiple compounds, including Quercitrin-7-olate, Armepavine, and romidepsin. These compounds all lead to the High-affinity choline transporter, suggesting a common mechanism of action involving the choline transporter. The integration of these pathways implies that Pironetin may exert its effects by modulating the activity of the choline transporter, potentially influencing cellular processes related to choline uptake and metabolism. The consistent targeting of CCRF-HSB-2 by these compounds supports the hypothesis that Pironetin interacts with the choline transporter through a shared biological mechanism, possibly involving the regulation of choline transport in the cell. This relationship highlights the importance of the choline transporter in the pharmacological profile of Pironetin and suggests a potential role in drug action that warrants further investigation.",
